## What happened

In January 2019 CMAX Foundation announced the launch of a public-private network for disaster risk reduction in Mexico: an alliance of private-sector organizations committed to disaster resilience, working with public institutions.

The network followed the first Social Innovation Lab for Emergencies (LISE), created with Universidad de Monterrey in 2018, whose first workshop took place in Oaxaca after the 2017 earthquakes.

## Documentation

The Foundation is adding participant lists, photographs and the founding documents of the network to this record. The original announcement is linked above.
